    - Week: the last 13 calendar weeks, plus "All 90 days".
    - Smallest diff, about 150–180 lines. Every type stays reachable.
    - Easy to change later.
  - [1mB: three radio buttons plus the week dropdown.[0m
    - The two shortcuts are visible without opening a menu.
    - You can't pick a single other type, such as only Sign-out.
    - The guidelines allow horizontal radios only for 2–3 short labels, so adding a fourth view later would mean
      switching to a dropdown.
  - [1mC: "Show" dropdown plus start date, end date and a presets dropdown.[0m
    - Any span of days, not just calendar weeks.
    - Four controls and the end-before-start validation from 03 add roughly 80–100 lines over A.
    - With only 90 days of history, it's more precision than "one particular week" needs.

  [1mMy recommendation:[0m A. It answers all three needs with the fewest controls, keeps all nine types reachable, and leaves
  room under the 300-line limit.

